WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.443
Welcome to Hisaab.

00:00:02.463 --> 00:00:07.746
Accounts, stock, GST, TDS and payroll, for
Indian businesses.

00:00:08.446 --> 00:00:10.839
Your books stay on your own computer.

00:00:10.859 --> 00:00:12.987
You need no account with us.

00:00:13.007 --> 00:00:15.090
And Hisaab is free.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:21.307
If you know Tally, you know Hisaab: the same
Gateway, the same keys, the same reports.

00:00:21.337 --> 00:00:23.953
Alt+K is still the company menu.

00:00:25.527 --> 00:00:31.276
GST invoices, printed, as PDF, by e-mail or on
WhatsApp.

00:00:32.356 --> 00:00:37.106
And your company comes over from Tally, with a
proof that every balance matches.

00:00:38.086 --> 00:00:42.903
This film has ten short chapters. Watch them
in order, or jump to the one you need.

00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:48.169
Chapter three: switch from Tally, with a proof
that every balance matches.

00:00:48.869 --> 00:00:53.062
First, one time in TallyPrime: turn on its XML
port.

00:00:53.082 --> 00:00:56.542
Press F1, then Settings, then Connectivity.

00:00:56.562 --> 00:01:01.890
Set "TallyPrime acts as" to Both. Set the port
to 9000, and press Ctrl+A.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:05.993
Then close TallyPrime, open it again, and open
your company.

00:01:06.793 --> 00:01:11.076
Now open Hisaab. On a new PC, the company list
is empty.

00:01:11.106 --> 00:01:15.990
Select Switch from Tally, and press Enter.
Hisaab looks for Tally at once.

00:01:16.688 --> 00:01:21.305
Esc shows the search. Hisaab looked on this PC
and in the office network.

00:01:21.335 --> 00:01:28.554
In this film, a test Tally answers on port
9260. Your TallyPrime uses port 9000.

00:01:28.584 --> 00:01:34.801
Enter shows each company that is open in
Tally, with its GSTIN, its dates and its vouchers.

00:01:35.881 --> 00:01:40.232
Space ticks a company. Press Enter, and Enter
again for Yes.

00:01:40.262 --> 00:01:46.813
Hisaab copies the masters, then the vouchers, in
parts. Esc stops it, and then nothing is saved.

00:01:47.893 --> 00:01:53.709
Enter opens the Proof of Match. Hisaab asks
Tally for its own reports, and compares every line.

00:01:53.739 --> 00:02:00.223
Ledger balances, stock, open bills, the Trial
Balance, Profit and Loss, and the Balance Sheet.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:04.805
Each line shows the value in Tally, the value
in Hisaab, and a tick.

00:02:04.835 --> 00:02:09.652
F5 shows only the differences. Here there are
none, so the switch is done.

00:02:09.682 --> 00:02:15.032
When a line differs, Enter shows its vouchers,
and F6 accepts the difference with a reason.

00:02:16.012 --> 00:02:24.140
What moves: groups and ledgers, stock items, every voucher
with its bills and GST details, payroll, TDS, and TCS.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:31.576
What does not move: users and passwords, Tally add-ons, print
designs, and the old edit log. Keep your Tally backup.

00:02:32.377 --> 00:02:37.794
Some people still enter bills in Tally for a
few days. Then open Import, Switch from Tally.

00:02:38.495 --> 00:02:44.777
Press S for Sync again. Only the changes come
over: here, one new invoice. The proof runs again.

00:02:45.857 --> 00:02:52.408
If the Tally PC has no network, press F,
and give the XML files that Tally exports with Alt+E.

00:02:53.388 --> 00:02:57.649
Hisaab only reads from Tally. Your Tally data
stays as it is.

00:02:57.669 --> 00:03:00.856
It works the same with a real TallyPrime. In
our test,

00:03:00.876 --> 00:03:05.421
Tally's sample company of 736 vouchers
switched in about twelve seconds.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:09.102
Chapter four: the Gateway and the keys.

00:03:09.902 --> 00:03:13.320
This is the Gateway of Hisaab. Your work
starts here.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:18.500
On the left: the current period, the current
date, your company, and its last backup.

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:23.616
On the right: the menu. Use the arrow keys, or
press the blue letter of an item.

00:03:24.316 --> 00:03:27.734
The top bar has the menus, from Company to
Help.

00:03:27.764 --> 00:03:31.115
The button bar on the right shows the keys of
each screen.

00:03:32.195 --> 00:03:38.679
Alt+K opens the Company menu: create, alter,
select or shut a company. Esc closes it.

00:03:38.709 --> 00:03:42.661
F2 changes the current date. New vouchers take
this date.

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:47.169
Ctrl+A accepts. The Gateway now shows 30 June.

00:03:48.249 --> 00:03:53.133
Alt+G is Go To. Type a part of a report name,
for example "trial".

00:03:53.163 --> 00:03:57.182
Enter opens the Trial Balance at once. Esc
brings you back.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:06.346
Alt+F is SmartFind. Type a name, a GSTIN, a
number or an amount. Small spelling mistakes are allowed.

00:04:06.376 --> 00:04:12.260
Esc twice, then D: Display More Reports. Every
report of Hisaab is in this list.

00:04:12.958 --> 00:04:17.842
The mouse works too: a click opens an item,
for example the Balance Sheet.

00:04:17.872 --> 00:04:21.555
But the keys are faster. Esc, and you are
back.

00:04:22.535 --> 00:04:26.528
Here are the ten keys that you need. Alt+K for
the company menu.

00:04:26.548 --> 00:04:30.208
Alt+F3 to select a company, F2 for the date.

00:04:30.228 --> 00:04:35.822
V for vouchers, Ctrl+A to accept, Esc to go
back, and Enter to open a line.

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:40.260
Alt+G to go to any report, Alt+F to find, and
F1 for help.

00:04:40.983 --> 00:04:45.535
Chapter five: daily work, with GST and TDS.

00:04:46.335 --> 00:04:50.287
V opens the vouchers. F8 is a sales invoice.

00:04:50.329 --> 00:04:55.479
Type a part of the party name, Sharma, and
press Enter. Then the sales ledger.

00:04:56.179 --> 00:05:02.995
Add each item and its quantity: 100 metres of
cotton fabric, and 10 kurtas. Hisaab fills the rate.

00:05:04.224 --> 00:05:12.510
Select CGST and SGST. Hisaab calculates the
tax from each item's rate: 790 rupees each.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:17.025
Type the narration, and press Enter. Hisaab
asks: Accept?

00:05:17.725 --> 00:05:23.810
Y for yes. Then the bill-wise details: a new
bill, number 4, due in 30 days.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:27.124
Enter on End of List, and the invoice is
saved.

00:05:28.875 --> 00:05:33.088
Page Up opens the invoice again, and Ctrl+P
shows the print preview:

00:05:33.108 --> 00:05:37.161
a GST tax invoice, with HSN codes and the
amount in words.

00:05:37.191 --> 00:05:43.276
From here, E exports a PDF, M sends it by
e-mail, and Alt+W sends it on WhatsApp.

00:05:44.356 --> 00:05:50.773
For a purchase, press F9. Type the supplier's
invoice number and date, the party, and the items.

00:05:55.133 --> 00:05:59.950
Mehta Fabrics is in Maharashtra, so Hisaab
takes IGST.

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:03.797
Narration, Y to accept, and the bill goes to
the payables.

00:06:08.143 --> 00:06:14.425
F6 is a receipt. The bank, the party, and the
amount: 24,080 rupees.

00:06:15.123 --> 00:06:19.075
Bill-wise: Agst Ref shows the open bills of
Sharma Traders.

00:06:19.105 --> 00:06:26.922
Pick invoice 4, type the narration, and Ctrl+A. The
bank details come next; Ctrl+A again saves the receipt.

00:06:28.672 --> 00:06:36.088
F5 is a payment: the bank, Mehta Fabrics, and
63,000 rupees. Agst Ref shows its open bill.

00:06:36.785 --> 00:06:42.736
Pick the bill, type the narration, then
Ctrl+A, the bank details, and Ctrl+A again.

00:06:43.435 --> 00:06:49.986
F4 is a contra: 20,000 rupees of cash,
deposited in the bank. Ctrl+A saves it.

00:06:53.025 --> 00:06:59.576
F7 is a journal. Rent, 60,000 rupees, debit.
Desai Properties, credit.

00:07:00.275 --> 00:07:07.691
Hisaab adds the TDS line by itself: ten
percent under section 194-I. The landlord gets 54,000.

00:07:07.721 --> 00:07:10.606
Narration, and Ctrl+A saves it.

00:07:14.364 --> 00:07:18.513
Esc, then K: the Day Book shows every voucher
of the day.

00:07:20.183 --> 00:07:24.399
Chapter six: reports. Enter always opens the
next level.

00:07:25.199 --> 00:07:28.749
K opens the Day Book: the vouchers of the
current date.

00:07:28.779 --> 00:07:31.597
Enter on a line opens the voucher itself.

00:07:33.164 --> 00:07:36.246
Esc back, and B shows the Balance Sheet.

00:07:36.945 --> 00:07:40.027
Select Current Assets, and press Enter.

00:07:40.728 --> 00:07:44.079
Then Sundry Debtors: the parties who owe you
money.

00:07:44.778 --> 00:07:48.129
Enter on a party shows its balance, month by
month.

00:07:48.159 --> 00:07:50.708
Enter on a month shows its vouchers,

00:07:51.408 --> 00:07:56.025
and Enter on a voucher opens it. Esc goes
back, one level at a time.

00:07:57.776 --> 00:08:02.727
P is the Profit and Loss account: the gross
profit, and the net result of the period.

00:08:03.807 --> 00:08:08.359
S is the Stock Summary: the quantity, the rate
and the value of each group.

00:08:08.389 --> 00:08:13.006
Enter on Fabrics, then on Cotton Fabric: its
movement, month by month.

00:08:14.424 --> 00:08:19.909
Alt+G, "receivable": the bills that customers still owe,
with the due date and the days overdue.

00:08:20.607 --> 00:08:25.890
Ctrl+E exports any report to Excel or PDF, and
Ctrl+P prints it.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:28.205
Esc, and you are back.

00:08:29.217 --> 00:08:33.366
Chapter seven: GST, TDS and payroll.

00:08:34.166 --> 00:08:41.385
Alt+G, GSTR-1: the outward supplies of the
month, table by table. Invoice 4 is in B2B.

00:08:41.415 --> 00:08:45.098
Alt+E exports the JSON file for the GST
portal.

00:08:45.128 --> 00:08:48.945
GSTR-3B comes from the same vouchers.

00:08:49.646 --> 00:08:57.463
For GSTR-2B, import the portal's file with Ctrl+I.
Hisaab matches each supplier invoice with your books.

00:08:58.543 --> 00:09:02.704
Alt+Z, W: the e-way bills. Hisaab lists each
invoice that needs one,

00:09:02.724 --> 00:09:06.893
and what to correct first: here, the PIN code
of the party.

00:09:06.923 --> 00:09:12.739
X writes the JSON file for the e-way
bill portal. With Hisaab Services, S sends it online.

00:09:13.819 --> 00:09:20.836
Form 26Q, now Form 140, collects the TDS of
the quarter: the rent, 6,000 rupees.

00:09:20.944 --> 00:09:26.429
Alt+X writes the e-TDS file. Check it with the
government's FVU before you upload it.

00:09:27.509 --> 00:09:30.659
Payroll: V, then Ctrl+F4.

00:09:31.358 --> 00:09:34.974
Ctrl+F fills the salary of every employee for
the month.

00:09:35.004 --> 00:09:40.489
Basic, HRA, PF and ESI come from each
employee's salary details.

00:09:40.519 --> 00:09:44.069
Then Ctrl+A, and the payroll voucher is saved.

00:09:44.771 --> 00:09:48.257
And the pay slips are ready: Alt+G, "pay
slip".

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:52.969
Chapter eight: safe data.

00:09:53.669 --> 00:09:59.064
On Windows, the books are in
Documents\Hisaab\Data: one folder for each company.

00:09:59.084 --> 00:10:04.170
Every day, and before every update, Hisaab
backs up every company by itself.

00:10:04.969 --> 00:10:08.854
Alt+Y opens the Data menu. Then Backup &
Restore.

00:10:09.075 --> 00:10:16.160
L is the Daily Backup. It is on from the first
day: every day, Hisaab backs up every company and keeps 7 versions.

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:24.207
A copy on this PC does not help when the PC is
lost. F9 sets up a copy outside: Google Drive, OneDrive, or a folder.

00:10:25.287 --> 00:10:29.969
For a backup now, press B in the same menu.
The company is selected.

00:10:29.999 --> 00:10:33.549
Ctrl+A, then Enter, takes the backup now.

00:10:34.248 --> 00:10:40.998
F8 sets a backup password. The file is then encrypted:
it opens only with that password or the recovery key.

00:10:42.078 --> 00:10:45.362
Hisaab Drive sends the backups to your own
cloud.

00:10:45.829 --> 00:10:53.514
F4 adds a place: Google Drive, OneDrive, or any
synced folder. Every backup is encrypted on this PC first.

00:10:54.594 --> 00:11:01.280
R restores a backup, as a new company or in place
of the old one. Hisaab always asks before it replaces anything.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:06.977
Alt+K, V: Hisaab Vault encrypts the whole
company with a password.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:12.230
Keep that password in a safe place: nobody can
recover it, not even us.

00:11:13.217 --> 00:11:15.833
Chapter ten: help and support.

00:11:16.633 --> 00:11:23.383
Not sure on a screen? Press F1: the
manual, the keyboard shortcuts, the settings and Hisaab Services.

00:11:23.413 --> 00:11:27.298
F1 again opens the manual page of the screen
you are on.

00:11:28.378 --> 00:11:32.863
Ctrl+K changes the screen language: Hindi,
Gujarati and more.

00:11:32.893 --> 00:11:38.109
Here is the Gateway in Gujarati. The keys stay
the same, and your data does not change.

00:11:38.139 --> 00:11:41.156
Ctrl+K again, and English is back.

00:11:42.905 --> 00:11:47.753
F1, V: Hisaab Services lists every online
service, like Connected GST,

00:11:47.773 --> 00:11:52.387
e-invoice and Hisaab Drive, and shows which
ones are set up.

00:11:53.367 --> 00:11:56.561
At each start, Hisaab checks for a new
version.

00:11:56.581 --> 00:12:01.331
F1, Upgrade installs it. Hisaab first backs up
every company.

00:12:02.031 --> 00:12:05.960
Questions? Write to info@nexertechnology.com.

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:11.066
Practise on the demo company first, then
switch your own books. Welcome to Hisaab.

